$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A Typical Procedure for the Leibeskind-Srogl
Coupling To Generate Compound 8a-e. In a 10 mL microwave vial the
following were successively added: compound 5a-d, 5g (0.2 mmol), THF (3
mL), boronic acid 6a-d (0.6 mmol, 3.0 equiv), Pd(PPh3)4 (11 mg, 5 mol %),
and CuTC (76 mg, 2 equiv). The reaction tube was sealed and irradiated at
a ceiling temperature of 110 °C using 200 W maximum power for 50 min.
After the reaction mixture was cooled with an air flow for 15 min, it was
extracted with dichloromethane (2 × 50 mL) and dried over MgSO4. The
solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the residue was subjected
to preparative HPLC column chromatography. The compound was purified by
reversed phase preparative HPLC using acetonitrile/water (with 0.1%
HCOOH) as the eluent. All gradients ran between 80:20:0.01
(water/acetonitrile/HCOOH) and 0:100:0.01 (water/acetonitrile/HCOOH) for
25 min, with the UV detector set at λ = 215 and 254 nm to afford compound
8a-e.
2-methoxy-5-(4-methoxyphenyl)-3-(3,4-dimethylphenyl)-6-(naphthalen-2-yl)pyrazine
(8c): 94% yield. yellow solid m.p. 154-156 °C. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ
8.21 (d, J = 9.6 Hz, 2H), 7.49 (d, J = 9.4 Hz, 2H), 7.46 – 7.41 (m, 4H),
7.33 (d, J = 9.2 Hz, 2H), 6.84 (d, J = 9.7 Hz, 2H), 4.14 (s, 3H), 3.83
(s, 3H), 1.32 (s, 9H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 159.5, 154.2, 151.8,
146.5, 143.8, 137.6, 135.1, 134.4, 131.6 (x 2C), 131.1 (x 2C), 129.5,
128.5 (x 2C), 125.3 (x 2C), 113.7 (x 2C), 55.4, 53.9, 34.8, 31.4 (x 3C).
HR-MS (EI): C30H26N2O2 calcd. 446.1994, found 446.1994.
