$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A Typical Procedure for the Suzuki Coupling To Generate Compound 5a-h. In
a 10 mL microwave vial the following were successively dissolved in
dioxane/H2O (1:1, 3 mL): halopyrazine 4a-c (0.3 mmol), boronic acid 6a-g
(0.36 mmol, 1.2 equiv), Pd(PPh3)4 (8 mg, 2 mol %), and K2CO3 (84 mg, 2
equiv). The reaction tube was sealed and irradiated at a ceiling
temperature of 120 °C using 150 W maximum power for 10 min. After the
reaction mixture was cooled with an air flow for 15 min, extracted with
dichloromethane (2 × 50 mL) and dried over MgSO4. The solvent was removed
under reduced pressure, and the residue was subjected to preparative HPLC
column chromatography. All the compounds were purified by reversed phase
preparative HPLC using acetonitrile/ water (with 0.1% HCOOH) as the
eluent. All gradients ran between 80:20:0.01 (water/acetonitrile/HCOOH)
and 0:100:0.01 (water/acetonitrile/HCOOH) for 20 min, with the UV
detector set at λ = 215 and 254 nm to afford compounds 5a-h.
3-Methoxy-5-(4-methoxyphenyl)-2-(methylthio)pyrazine (5a): 92% yield.
white crystalline solid. Mp 95-97 °C. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.39 (s,
1H), 7.92 (d, J = 9.9 Hz, 2H), 6.97 (d, J = 9.9 Hz, 2H), 4.09 (s, 3H),
3.85 (s, 3H), 2.56 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 160.5, 155.8,
143.8, 143.6, 131.6, 129.0, 127.6, 114.3, 55.5, 53.8, 12.1. HR-MS (EI):
C13H14N2O2S calcd 262.0776, found 262.0772.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Novel and Versatile Entry to Asymmetrically Substituted Pyrazines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mehta, Vaibhav Pravinchandra; Sharma, Anuj; Van Hecke, Kristof; Van
Meervelt, Luc; Van der Eycken, Erik
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2008), 73(6), 2382-2388

