$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Preparation of 3 (3a
for Example). To a 50 mL three-necked round-bottomed flask equipped with
a magnetic stir bar were added 1a (111 mg, 0.5 mmol), 2a (122 mg, 1.0
mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (29 mg, 0.025 mmol), and CuTC (143 mg, 0.75 mmol) under
an atmosphere of N2. Then, 1,4-dioxane (5 mL) was added to the mixture by
using a syringe, and the resultant mixture was stirred at 90 °C for 12 h
to consume the starting materials as indicated by TLC. The resulting
mixture was filtered through Buchner funnel. The filtrate was poured into
saturated aqueous NaCl (10 mL) and extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 × 10 mL). The
combined organic phase was washed with water (3 × 10 mL), dried over
MgSO4, and concentrated in vacuum. The residue was purified by flash
silica gel chromatography (petroleum ether/ethyl acetate = 40/1, v/v).
1-(5-Hydroxy-2-phenylbenzofuran-3-yl)-ethanone (3a). Yield: 85%, White
solid. Condition: Time: 14 h, Solvent: THF. mp 207-209 °C; 1H NMR (500
MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 2.27 (s, 3H), 6.83-6.85 (m, 1H), 7.43-7.44 (m, 1H),
7.47-7.48 (m, 1H), 7.55-7.59 (m, 3H), 7.78-7.80 (m, 2H), 9.46 (s, 1H);
13C NMR (125 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 30.7, 107.0, 112.1, 114.7, 118.2, 127.6,
129.1 (2C), 130.1 (2C), 130.3, 131.1, 148.0, 155.0, 161.1, 195.0; HRMS
(ESI-TOF): calcd for C16H13O3 253.0859 (M+H+), found 253.0868.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study, optimized on time and temperature, Liebeskind-Srogl
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pd-Catalyzed C-S Activation for [3 + 3] Annulation of
2-(Methylthio)benzofuran-3-carboxylates and 2-(Hydroxyphenyl)boronic
Acids: Synthesis of Coumestan Derivatives
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
