$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM BODIPY 20. An oven-dry Schlenk tube, equipped with a stir bar, was
charged with 8- (3,5-dibromophenyl)bodipy 11 (30 mg, 70.5 μmol, 1 equiv),
4- (diphenylamino)phenylboronic acid (122 mg, 0.423 mmol, 6 equiv),
Na2CO3 (90 mg, 0.845 mmol, 12 equiv) and DME/H2O (4/1, 5 mL) under N2.
The stirred solution was sparged with N2 for 10 min., whereupon Pd(PPh3)4
(9.8 mg, 8.45 μmol, 12 mol%) was added followed by 5 min N2-purge. The
reaction mixture was heated at 80 °C. The reaction was monitored by TLC
(Rf = 0.24, SiO2-gel, 20% EtOAc/hexanes), which showed that the reaction
was finished after 20 min. The reaction mixture was allowed to reach room
temperature and was adsorbed on SiO2-gel. After flash-chromatography
(SiO2-gel, EtOAc/hexanes gradient) purification, followed by
recrystallization from petroleum ether/toluene, 20 (44 mg, 58.2 μmol,
83%) was obtained as a deep red solid. BODIPY 20, yield (44 mg, 58.2
μmol, 83%) Mp: 149-151 °C; IR (KBr, cm-1) 3034 (w), 1590 (s), 1555 (s),
1509 (s), 1489 (s), 1411 (s), 1386 (s), 1261 (s), 1113 (s), 1075 (s), 753
(m), 695 (m); 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 7.96 (s, 2H), 7.67 (d, J = 1.6
Hz, 2H), 7.53 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 4H), 7.32-7.01 (m, 27H), 6.57-6.55 (m, 2H);
13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 148.2, 147.6, 144.4, 141.7, 135.2, 135.0,
133.5, 131.8, 129.6, 128.1, 127.4, 127.2, 124.9, 123.7, 123.5, 118.8;
HRMS FABS (M+H+) Calcd for C51H38BF2N4: 755.3158. Found: 755.3155.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel meso-Polyarylamine-BODIPY Hybrids: Synthesis and Study of Their
Optical Properties
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Lager, Erik; Liu, Jianzhao; Aguilar-Aguilar, Angelica; Tang, Ben Zhong;
Pena-Cabrera, Eduardo
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2009), 74(5), 2053-2058

