$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A Typical Procedure for the Suzuki Coupling To
Generate Compound 5a-h. In a 10 mL microwave vial the following were
successively dissolved in dioxane/H2O (1:1, 3 mL): halopyrazine 4a-c (0.3
mmol), boronic acid 6a-g (0.36 mmol, 1.2 equiv), Pd(PPh3)4 (8 mg, 2 mol
%), and K2CO3 (84 mg, 2 equiv). The reaction tube was sealed and
irradiated at a ceiling temperature of 120 °C using 150 W maximum power
for 10 min. After the reaction mixture was cooled with an air flow for 15
min, extracted with dichloromethane (2 × 50 mL) and dried over MgSO4. The
solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the residue was subjected
to preparative HPLC column chromatography. All the compounds were
purified by reversed phase preparative HPLC using acetonitrile/ water
(with 0.1% HCOOH) as the eluent. All gradients ran between 80:20:0.01
(water/acetonitrile/HCOOH) and 0:100:0.01 (water/acetonitrile/HCOOH) for
20 min, with the UV detector set at λ = 215 and 254 nm to afford
compounds 5a-h.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Novel and Versatile Entry to Asymmetrically Substituted Pyrazines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
