$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A Typical Procedure for the Leibeskind-Srogl Coupling To Generate
Compound 8a-e. In a 10 mL microwave vial the following were successively
added: compound 5a-d, 5g (0.2 mmol), THF (3 mL), boronic acid 6a-d (0.6
mmol, 3.0 equiv), Pd(PPh3)4 (11 mg, 5 mol %), and CuTC (76 mg, 2 equiv).
The reaction tube was sealed and irradiated at a ceiling temperature of
110 °C using 200 W maximum power for 50 min. After the reaction mixture
was cooled with an air flow for 15 min, it was extracted with
dichloromethane (2 × 50 mL) and dried over MgSO4. The solvent was removed
under reduced pressure, and the residue was subjected to preparative HPLC
column chromatography. The compound was purified by reversed phase
preparative HPLC using acetonitrile/water (with 0.1% HCOOH) as the
eluent. All gradients ran between 80:20:0.01 (water/acetonitrile/HCOOH)
and 0:100:0.01 (water/acetonitrile/HCOOH) for 25 min, with the UV
detector set at λ = 215 and 254 nm to afford compound 8a-e.
2-(3-Ethoxyphenyl)-3-methoxy-5-(4-methoxyphenyl)pyrazine (8a): 82% yield.
White crystalline solid. Mp 102-104 °C. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.64
(s, 1H), 8.04 (d, J = 9.5 Hz, 2H), 7.71-7.67 (m, 2H), 7. 39-7.34 (t, J =
8.7 Hz, 1H), 7.01 (d, J = 9.9 Hz, 2H), 6.97-6.93 (dd, 1H), 4.15-4.08 (m,
2H), 4.12 (s, 3H), 3.86 (s, 3H), 1.46-1.41 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR
(75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 161.0, 158.9, 157.1, 147.3, 139.9, 137.3, 132.1,
129.2, 128.7, 128.1 (× 2C), 121.5, 115.5, 114.9, 114.4 (× 2C), 63.6,
55.5, 53.5, 14.9. HR-MS (EI): C20H20N2O3 calcd 336.1474, found 336.1470.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Liebeskind-Srogl coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Novel and Versatile Entry to Asymmetrically Substituted Pyrazines
