$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A typical procedure for the arylation of 3
with arylboronic acids - Synthesis of 4-phenyl-4-p-tolyl-but-3-en-2-one
(4g): Under nitrogen atmosphere, a mixture of 3aa (103 mg, 0.5 mmol),
arylboronic acid 2d (102 mg, 0.75 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (43 mg, 0.0375 mmol),
dppe (15 mg, 0.0375 mmol), CuTC (191 mg, 1.0 mmol) and K2CO3 (138 mg, 1.0
mmol) in 5 mL THF was stirred at 50°C for 13 h. After cooled to ambient
temperature, the resulting mixture was filtered through a short pad of
celite and rinsed with 10 mL CH2Cl2. The combined filtrate was evaporated
all the volatiles under reduced pressure. The resultant residue was
purified by flash silica gel column chromatography (eluent : petroleum
ether (60-90°C)/EtOAc = 30:1, v/v) to afford the product.
(Z/E)-4-[1-(4-Chloro-phenyl)-3-oxo-3-phenyl-propenyl]-benzaldehyde
((Z/E)-4p) as a yellow liquid, yield 80%. 1H NMR (DMSO-d6, 400 MHz) δ for
(Z)-4p: 9.94 (s, 1 H, CHO), 7.89 and 7.46 (d each, J = 6.6 and 6.4 Hz,
2:2 H, aromatic CH), 7.81 and 7.26 (d each, J = 7.9 Hz, 2:2 H, aromatic
CH), 7.56 and 7.44 (m each, 2:3 H, CH of Ph), 7.36 (s, 1 H, CH=C-C6H4Cl);
for (E)-4p: 9.99 (s, 1 H, CHO), 7.87 and 7.56 (d each, J = 6.8 and 6.7
Hz, 2:2 H, aromatic CH), 7.31 and 7.06 (d each, J = 8.2 Hz, 2:2 H,
aromatic CH), 7.56 and 7.44 (m each, 2:3 H, CH of Ph), 7.34 (s, 1 H,
CH=C-C6H4Cl). 13C{1H} NMR (DMSO-d6, 100 MHz) δ for (Z)-4p: 193.1 (Cq,
CHO), 191.5 (Cq, C=O), 151.1 (Cq, CH=C-C6H4Cl), 145.4, 138.8, 137.7,
135.8 and 134.9 (Cq each, aromatic C), 133.6, 131.4, 130.2, 129.7, 129.1
and 128.8 (aromatic CH), 125.5 (CH=C-C6H4Cl); for (E)-4p: 193.1 (Cq,
CHO), 192.2 (Cq, C=O), 150.4 (Cq, CH=C-C6H4Cl), 146.0, 137.5, 137.4,
136.6 and 133.4 (Cq each, aromatic C), 133.7, 130.2, 130.0, 129.2, 129.1,
128.9 and 128.6 (aromatic CH), 127.4 (CH=C-C6H4Cl). HRMS Cacld for
C22H15O2Cl: 346.0761; Found: 346.0767.
