$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of Derivatives
10. A solution of boronic acid derivative (0.25 mmol), 8e (89.0 mg, 0.24
mmol), cesium carbonate (237.8 mg, 0.73 mmol), and Pd(PPh3)4 (11.6 mg,
0.01 mmol) in dioxane (2 mL) was heated at 90 °C under inert atmosphere.
After 3.5-7 h, the reaction mixture was cooled to rt and filtered through
Celite. The filtrate was evaporated under reduced pressure. The residue
was diluted with DCM (15 mL), washed with water (10 mL), brine (10 mL),
and dried over Na2SO4 . After evaporation of the solvents under vacuum at
40 °C, the resulting solid was suspended in MeOH, filtered, washed twice
with MeOH and once with diethyl ether, and dried under suction to afford
derivatives 10a-10c.
2-Diethylamino-4,8-diphenylpyrido[3,2-d]pyrimidine-6-carbox-\ylic acid
methyl ester (10a): yield = 80%; yellow solid. mp 133-134 °C; IR νmax
1555, 1240 cm-1; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δH 1.24-1.29 (m, 6H), 3.76 (br
m, 4H), 4.01 (s, 3H), 7.45-7.52 (m, 3H), 7.56-7.58 (m, 3H), 7.90-7.93 (m,
2H), 8.36 (s, 1H), 8.52-8.55 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (75.47 MHz, CDCl3) δC 13.4,
14.2, 42.9, 53.2, 127.2, 128.2, 128.4, 128.9, 130.7, 131.1, 132.3, 134.8,
136.8, 137.1, 142.0, 145.0, 149.9, 158.5, 166.3, 168.2; HPLC tR = 5.16
min; ES-MS m/z 345.99 (M + H)+. Anal. Calcd for C25H24N4O2 : C, 72.80; H,
5.86; N, 13.58. Found: C, 72.40; H, 5.82; N, 13.35.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
