$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure (GP) for the syntheses of
3-12 (Liebeskind-Srogl Crosscoupling) BODIPY 3. An oven-dry round bottom
flask, equipped with a stir bar, was charged with thiomethylbodipy 1 (40
mg, 0.168 mmol, 1 equiv), 4-(diphenylamino)phenylboronic acid (146 mg,
0.504 mmol, 3 equiv) and anhydrous THF (20 mL) under N2. The stirred
solution was sparged with N2 for 10 min., whereupon Pd2dba3 (3.8 mg, 4.2
μmol, 2.5 mol%), tri(2-furyl)phosphine (2.9 mg, 12.6 μmol, 7.5 mol%) and
copper(I) thiophene-2-carboxylate (96 mg, 0.504 mmol, 3 equiv) were added
followed by 5 min N2-purge. The reaction mixture was heated at 55 °C. The
reaction was monitored by TLC (Rf = 0.44, SiO2-gel, 20% EtOAc/hexanes),
which showed that the reaction was finished after 1.5 h. The reaction
mixture was allowed to reach r.t. and was adsorbed on SiO2-gel. After
flash chromatography (SiO2-gel, EtOAc/hexanes gradient) purification,
followed by washings with petroleum ether (3 x 2 mL), 3 (72 mg, 0.165
mmol, 98%) was obtained as a purple solid 6, yield 78%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel meso-Polyarylamine-BODIPY Hybrids: Synthesis and Study of Their
Optical Properties
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Lager, Erik; Liu, Jianzhao; Aguilar-Aguilar, Angelica; Tang, Ben Zhong;
Pena-Cabrera, Eduardo
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2009), 74(5), 2053-2058

