$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure 1: To a stirred mixture of
5,17-bis(methylsulfanyl)oxacalix[2]arene[2]pyrimidine 1 (100 mg, 0.20
mmol) and Pd(PPh3)4 (12 mg, 5 mol%) in THF (5 mL) under Ar, the
respective arylboronic acid 2a–d (0.61 mmol, 3 equiv) and CuTC (139 mg,
0.71 mmol, 3.5 equiv) were added, and the resulting mixture was heated at
reflux for 24 h under an Ar atmosphere. After cooling to rt, THF was
evaporated in vacuum and the residue was dissolved in CH2Cl2, washed with
distilled water and the organic fraction was dried over MgSO4 and
filtered. The respective oxacalix[4]arenes 3a–d were purified by column
chromatography (silica) and obtained as white solids.
4,6,16,18-tetraaza-11,23-dimethyl-5,17-bis(4-methoxyphenyl)-2,8,14,20-tetraoxacalix[4]arene
(3b): 4-Methoxyphenylboronic acid (2b) (93 mg, 0.61 mmol); Eluent
CH2Cl2-heptane 4-1; Yield 78% (97 mg) mp >325 °C; MS (APCI+) m/z 613.6
[MH+]; HRMS (EI) calcd for C36H28N4O6: 612.2009; found: m/z 612.2008; 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.45 (d, J = 9.1 Hz, 4H; m-CH3O-Ph), 6.99 (d, J
=9.1 Hz, 4H; o-CH3O-Ph), 6.94 (d, J = 1.2 Hz, 4H; 4,6-orc), 6.69 (s, 2H;
2-orc), 5.28 (s, 2H; 5-pyr), 3.89 (s, 6H; CH3-O), 2.40 (s, 6H; CH3-orc);
13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 173.0 (C; 4,6-pyr), 166.3 (C; 2-pyr), 162.8 (C;
i-MeO-Ph), 153.1 (C; 1,3-orc), 143.8 (C; 5-orc), 130.7 (CH; m-MeO-Ph),
128.6 (C; p-MeO-Ph), 120.6 (CH; 4,6-orc), 114.0 (CH; o-MeO-Ph), 111.8
(CH; 2-orc), 84.7 (CH; 5-pyr), 55.6 (CH3;OMe), 21.7 (CH3; orc).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient Post-Macrocyclization Functionalizations of
Oxacalix[2]arene[2]pyrimidines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
