$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Copper
10-(4,6-diphenylpyrimidin-5-yl)-5,15-bis(2,4,6-trimethylphenyl)corrole
(8): To a mixture of Cu-corrole 6a (50 mg, 0.067 mmol) and Pd(PPh3)4 (4
mg, 5 mol%) in toluene (5 mL) under Ar, phenylboronic acid (25 mg, 0.205
mmol, 3 equiv) was added, immediately followed by the addition of aq
Na2CO3 (2M, 0.5 mL). The mixture was heated at reflux for 24 h under an
Ar atmosphere. After cooling to rt, the solvent was evaporated in vacuum
and the residue was dissolved in CH2Cl2, washed with distilled water and
the organic layer was dried over MgSO4 and filtered. The solvent was
evaporated in vacuum and the crude corrole was purified by column
chromatography (silica, eluent CH2Cl2−ethyl acetate 10−1), affording 42
mg (75%) of corrole 8 as a red-brown solid.6 Copper
10-(4,6-diphenylpyrimidin-5-yl)-5,15-bis(2,4,6-trimethylphenyl)corrole
(8): , yield 42 mg 75% MS (ESI+) m/z 825.4 [MH+]; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 9.50 (s, 1H, Hpyrim.), 7.88 (sbr, 2H, Hβ), 7.44−7.36 (m, 6H), 7.15−7.09
(m, 6H), 6.99 (d, 3J = 4.6 Hz, 2H, Hβ), 6.94 (s, 4H, Hmesit.), 6.88 (dbr,
3J = 4.6 Hz, 2H, Hβ), 2.37 (s, 6H), 1.89 (s, 12H); 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 158.1 (CHpyrim.), 150.0, 144.5, 144.1, 138.3, 137.7, 137.2,
130.7 (CH), 129.0 (CH), 128.2 (CH), 128.1 (CH), 127.9 (CH), 121.0 (CH),
21.2 (CH3), 19.6 (CH3); UV–vis (CH2Cl2) λmax (log ε) 264 (4.587), 423
(4.803), 547 (3.899), 660 (3.484).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
