$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Liebeskind-Srogl Coupling Reaction; General Procedure E To the N-3
protected imidazolinone (1 mmol, 1 equiv), dissolved in anhyd THF (10 mL)
under argon were added Pd(PPh3)4 (0.1 mmol, 0.1 equiv), copper(I)
thiophene-2-carboxylate (CuTC) (3 mmol, 3 equiv), and
4-methoxyphenylboronic acid (1.2 mmol, 1.2 equiv) at r.t. The mixture was
stirred for 24 h at 70°C, after which the solution was diluted with EtOAc
(20 mL), and washed with sat. aq NaHCO3 (3 × 50 mL). The combined organic
layers were filtered over Celite and concentrated in vacuo. The crude
product was purified by flash silica gel column chromatography (Table 3).
(4Z)-1-Benzyloxycarbonyl-4-(4-methoxybenzylidene)-2-(4-
methoxyphenyl)-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-5-one (16c) Compound 13 (100 mg,
0.22 mmol, 1 equiv) was submitted to the coupling reaction according to
general procedure E. Flash chromatographic purification (PE-EtOAc, 8:2).
The imidazolone 16c as a yellow solid; yield: 67 mg (69%). mp 126-128°C;
Rf = 0.34 (PE-EtOAc, 7:3). IR (neat): 1735.9 (C=O), 1597.0-1502.9 (C=C),
1250.8-1170.3 cm-1 (C-N). 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ = 3.85, 3.86 (2 s, 6 H,
OCH3), 5.33 (s, 2 H, CH2OCO), 6.89 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2 Harom), 6.96 (d, J =
8.8 Hz, 2 Harom), 7.23 (s, 1 H, H-6), 7.59 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2 Harom), 7.34
(s, 5 H, C6H5), 8.19 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2 Harom). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ = 55.4
(2 × OCH3), 69.6 (CH2OCO), 113.6 (CHaryl), 114.4 (CHaryl), 122.1 (Caryl),
126.8 (Caryl), 128.5, 128.6 (CHphenyl), 130.0 (C-6), 130.0 (CHaryl),
134.1 (Cphenyl), 134.7 (CHaryl), 135.0 (C-4), 149.5 (OC=O), 156.8 (C-2),
162.0 (4-MeOC arom), 161.8 (4-MeOC arom), 167.07 (C-5). MS (IS): m/z =
399.0 [M - CO2 + H]+, 443.5 [M + H]+, 465.0 [M + Na]+. HRMS-ES: m/z [M -
CO2 + H]+ calcd for C25H23N2O3: 399.17032; found: 399.17032; [M + H]+
calcd for C26H23N2O5: 443.16015; found: 443.16031; [M + Na]+ calcd for
C26H22N2O5 + Na: 465.14209; found: 465.14207.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Liebeskind-Srogl reaction, sealed vial used
