$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: BODIPY 20. An oven-dry Schlenk tube, equipped
with a stir bar, was charged with 8- (3,5-dibromophenyl)bodipy 11 (30 mg,
70.5 μmol, 1 equiv), 4- (diphenylamino)phenylboronic acid (122 mg, 0.423
mmol, 6 equiv), Na2CO3 (90 mg, 0.845 mmol, 12 equiv) and DME/H2O (4/1, 5
mL) under N2. The stirred solution was sparged with N2 for 10 min.,
whereupon Pd(PPh3)4 (9.8 mg, 8.45 μmol, 12 mol%) was added followed by 5
min N2-purge. The reaction mixture was heated at 80 °C. The reaction was
monitored by TLC (Rf = 0.24, SiO2-gel, 20% EtOAc/hexanes), which showed
that the reaction was finished after 20 min. The reaction mixture was
allowed to reach room temperature and was adsorbed on SiO2-gel. After
flash-chromatography (SiO2-gel, EtOAc/hexanes gradient) purification,
followed by recrystallization from petroleum ether/toluene, 20 (44 mg,
58.2 μmol, 83%) was obtained as a deep red solid. BODIPY 21 was
synthesized according to the same procedure as BODIPY 20. The reaction
finished in 90 min. After chromatography the residue was recrystallized
from petroleum ether/toluene to yield 21, yield= 69%; TLC (20%
EtOAc/hexanes, Rf = 0.6); purple solid; mp: 235 °C (dec); IR (KBr, cm-1)
1611 (m), 1560 (s), 1523 (s), 1409 (m), 1387 (s), 1357 (m), 1263 (m),
1118 (s), 1073 (s), 1043 (w), 820 (w); 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3) δ:
7.95-7.92 (m, 3H), 7.55-7.62 (m, 6H), 7.10 (m, 2H); 6.85 (d, J = 8.0 Hz,
4H); 6.55 (m, 2H); 3.01 (s, 12H); 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 150.5,
148.3, 144.1, 142.0, 135.3, 134.8, 132.0, 128.1, 126.7, 126.3, 118.6,
113.0, 40.7. HRMS FABS (M+H+) Calcd for C31H30BF2N4: 507.2532. Found:
507.2535.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel meso-Polyarylamine-BODIPY Hybrids: Synthesis and Study of Their
Optical Properties
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Lager, Erik; Liu, Jianzhao; Aguilar-Aguilar, Angelica; Tang, Ben Zhong;
Pena-Cabrera, Eduardo
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2009), 74(5), 2053-2058

