$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A typical procedure for the arylation of 3 with arylboronic acids -
Synthesis of 4-phenyl-4-p-tolyl-but-3-en-2-one (4g): Under nitrogen
atmosphere, a mixture of 3aa (103 mg, 0.5 mmol), arylboronic acid 2d (102
mg, 0.75 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (43 mg, 0.0375 mmol), dppe (15 mg, 0.0375
mmol), CuTC (191 mg, 1.0 mmol) and K2CO3 (138 mg, 1.0 mmol) in 5 mL THF
was stirred at 50°C for 13 h. After cooled to ambient temperature, the
resulting mixture was filtered through a short pad of celite and rinsed
with 10 mL CH2Cl2. The combined filtrate was evaporated all the volatiles
under reduced pressure. The resultant residue was purified by flash
silica gel column chromatography (eluent : petroleum ether
(60-90°C)/EtOAc = 30:1, v/v) to afford the product.
4-Phenyl-4-p-tolyl-but-3-en-2-one (4g) as a yellow oil, yield 73 mg, 65%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Z:E = 50:50
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Regio- and Stereoselective Synthesis of Multisubstituted Olefins and
Conjugate Dienes by Using α-Oxo Ketene Dithioacetals as the Building
Blocks
