$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A typical procedure for the cross-coupling
reactions of 1 with aryl- and alkenylboronic acids 2 - Synthesis of
(E)-4-ethylsulfanyl-4-phenyl-but-3-en-2-one (3aa): Under nitrogen
atmosphere, a mixture of α-oxo ketene dithioacetal 1a (95 mg, 0.5 mmol),
arylboronic acid 2a (91 mg, 0.75 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (43 mg, 0.0375 mmol),
CuTC (191 mg, 1.0 mmol) and Cs2CO3 (326 mg, 1.0 mmol) in 5 mL THF stirred
at 50°C for 2 h. After cooled to ambient temperature, the resulting
mixture was filtered through a short pad of celite and rinsed with 10 mL
CH2Cl2. The combined filtrate was evaporated all the volatiles under
reduced pressure. The resultant residue was purified by flash silica gel
column chromatography (eluent : petroleum ether (60-90°C)/EtOAc = 30:1,
v/v) to afford the product.
(E)-4-(2-Methoxylphenyl)-4-(ethylthio)but-3-en-2-one ((E)-3ae) as a
yellow liquid, yield 63%. 1H NMR (acetone-d6, 400 MHz) δ 7.41, 7.20, 7.08
and 7.03 (m each, 1:1:1:1 H, aromatic CH), 6.16 (s, 1 H, CH=C-S), 3.84
(s, 3 H, OCH3), 2.85 (q, 2 H, SCH2), 1.79 (s, 3 H, CH3CO), 1.32 (t, 3 H,
SCH2CH3); 13C{1H} NMR (acetone-d6, 100 MHz) δ 194.8 (Cq, C=O), 157.6 (Cq,
aromatic C-OMe), 154.4 (Cq, CSEt), 131.7, 131.1, 123.8 and 121.8
(aromatic CH), 128.0 (Cq, aromatic C-CSEt), 112.7 (CH=C-S), 56.5 (OCH3),
30.0 (COCH3), 27.4 (SCH2), 13.8 (SCH2CH3). HRMS Cacld for C13H16O2S:
236.0871; Found: 236.0873.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Regio- and Stereoselective Synthesis of Multisubstituted Olefins and
Conjugate Dienes by Using α-Oxo Ketene Dithioacetals as the Building
Blocks
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
