$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Liebeskind-Srogl Coupling Reaction; General
Procedure E To the N-3 protected imidazolinone (1 mmol, 1 equiv),
dissolved in anhyd THF (10 mL) under argon were added Pd(PPh3)4 (0.1
mmol, 0.1 equiv), copper(I) thiophene-2-carboxylate (CuTC) (3 mmol, 3
equiv), and 4-methoxyphenylboronic acid (1.2 mmol, 1.2 equiv) at r.t. The
mixture was stirred for 24 h at 70°C, after which the solution was
diluted with EtOAc (20 mL), and washed with sat. aq NaHCO3 (3 × 50 mL).
The combined organic layers were filtered over Celite and concentrated in
vacuo. The crude product was purified by flash silica gel column
chromatography (Table 3).
(4Z)-1-Benzyloxycarbonyl-4-(4-methoxybenzylidene)-2-(4-
methoxyphenyl)-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-5-one (16c) Compound 13 (100 mg,
0.22 mmol, 1 equiv) was submitted to the coupling reaction according to
general procedure E. Flash chromatographic purification (PE-EtOAc, 8:2).
(4Z)-1-Benzyl-4-(4-methoxybenzylidene-2-(4-methoxyphenyl)-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-5-one
(16d) Compound 14 (150 mg, 0.36 mmol, 1 equiv) was submitted to the
coupling reaction according to general procedure E. Flash chromatographic
purification (PE-EtOAc, 8:2). The imidazolone 16d as a yellow solid;
yield: 90 mg (62%). mp 90-92°C; Rf = 0.24 (PE-EtOAc, 7:3). IR (neat):
1704.1 (C=O ring), 1502.2-1596.8 (N=CS), 1250.0- 1176.2 cm-1 (C-N). 1H
NMR (CDCl3): δ = 3.83, 3.85 (2 s, 6 H, OCH3), 4.97 (s, 2 H, NCH2), 6.91
(d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2 Harom), 6.95 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2 Harom), 7.17 (m, 2 H,
C6H5), 7.29 (s, 1 H, H-6), 7.54 (m, 3 H, C6H5), 7.65 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2
Harom), 8.23 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2 Harom). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ = 45.3 (NCH2),
55.3, 55.4 (OCH3), 114.1 (CHaryl), 114.3 (CHaryl), 121.7 (Caryl), 127.4
(C-4), 126.5, 127.5, 128.8 (CHphenyl), 128.3 (C-6), 130.3 (CHaryl), 134.4
(CHaryl), 136.8 (Cphenyl), 136.9 (CHaryl), 161.1 (C-2), 161.4 (4-MeOC
aryl), 162.0 (4- MeOC aryl), 171.9 (C-5). MS (IS): m/z = 399.0 [M + H]+,
421.0 [M + Na]+. HRMS-ES: m/z [M + H]+ calcd for C25H23N2O3: 399.17032;
found: 399.17054.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Liebeskind-Srogl reaction, optimized on catalyst, yield depends on
catalyst amount, boiling DMF/solvent,microwave irradn. gave lower yield,
sealed vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Thiohydantoins: selective N- and S-functionalization for Liebeskind-Srogl
reaction study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gosling, Sandrine; Rollin, Patrick; Tatibouet, Arnaud
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2011), (22), 3649-3660

