$DATUM Copper
10-[4,6-dichloro-2-(p-cyanophenyl)pyrimidin-5-yl]-5,15-bis(2,4,6-trimethylphenyl)-
corrole (10): To a mixture of Cu-corrole 6d (25.0 mg, 0.032 mmol) and
Pd(PPh3)4 (1.8 mg, 5 mol%) in THF (5 mL) under Ar, 4-cyanophenylboronic
acid (9.4 mg, 0.064 mmol, 2 equiv) and CuTC (12.2 mg, 0.064 mmol, 2
equiv) were added, and the resulting mixture was heated at reflux for 24
h under an Ar atmosphere. After cooling to rt, the solvent was evaporated
in vacuum and the residue was dissolved in CH2Cl2, washed with distilled
water and the organic layer was dried over MgSO4 and filtered. The crude
corrole was purified by column chromatography (silica, eluent
CH2Cl2−heptane 1−1), affording 16.6 mg (61%) of corrole 10 as a red-brown
solid. Copper
10-[4,6-dichloro-2-(p-cyanophenyl)pyrimidin-5-yl]-5,15-bis(2,4,6-trimethylphenyl)-
corrole (10): , yield 16.6 mg 61% MS (ESI+) m/z 843.2 [MH+]; 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.66 (d, 3J = 8.6 Hz, 2H), 8.00 (sbr, 2H, Hβ), 7.83 (d, 3J
= 8.3 Hz, 2H), 7.36 (d, 3J = 3.5 Hz, 2H, Hβ), 7.21 (sbr, 2H, Hβ), 7.02
(s, 4H, Hmesit.), 6.92 (d, 3J = 4.0 Hz, 2H, Hβ), 2.40 (s, 6H), 2.08 (s,
12H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 162.4, 148.7, 144.2 (br, Cα), 138.7,
138.2 (br, Cα), 137.8, 132.7 (CHβ), 132.6 (CH), 129.4 (CH), 128.2
(CHmesit.), 121.4 (CHβ), 118.4, 115.5, 21.2 (CH3), 19.8 (CH3); UV−vis
(CH2Cl2) λmax (log ε) 281 (4.798), 400 (4.962), 535 (4.020).
