$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Suzuki cross-coupling reaction of 12. An oven-dry Schlenk tube containing
a stir-bar, was charged with 4-biphenylboronic acid (17.1 mg, 0.09 mmol),
Pd(PPh3)4 (1.99 mg, 0.002 mmol), and K3PO4 (24.4 mg, 0.12 mmol) whereupon
a 6:1 (v:v) DME: H2O mixture (3 mL) was added. N2 was bubbled through the
solution for 5 min and then bodipy 12 (20.0 mg, 0.06 mmol) was added. The
reaction container was then immersed into a pre-heated oil-bath at 80 °C
for 1 h. The reaction mixture was cooled to rt and the solvent was
removed under reduced pressure. The crude material was purified by
gravity column chromatography (SiO2-gel, AcOEt/hexanes gradient) to give
23 as an orangegreen crystalline solid (14.4 mg, 59%). TLC (20%
EtOAc/hexanes, R f = 0.4); mp > 220 ºC; IR (KBr, cm-1) 3113 (w), 3033
(w), 2919 (w), 1551 (s), 1558 (s), 1412 (s), 1387 (s), 1263 (s), 1159
(m), 1117 (s), 10079 (s), 1050 (m), 977 (m); 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.97 (s, 2H), 7.83-7.66 (m, 10H), 7.52-7.39 (m, 3H), 7.03 (d, J= 4.0 Hz,
2H), 6.58 (d, J= 2.4 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3) δ 147.3, 144.3,
143.5, 141.3, 140.6, 138.8, 135.1, 133.0, 131.8, 131.4, 129.1, 128.0,
127.8, 127.8, 127.3, 127.2, 118.7; HRMS (C27H19BF2N2): calcd. 420.1609,
found 420.1602
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Simple, general, and efficient synthesis of meso-substituted
borondipyrromethenes from a single platform
